@startuml state_machines_wifi_dns
!theme cyborg
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam state {
 BackgroundColor #16324a
 BorderColor #4aa3df
 FontColor #e6edf7
 BackgroundColor<<terminal>> #3a1d22
 BorderColor<<terminal>> #e06c75
 BackgroundColor<<finding>> #3a2a12
 BorderColor<<finding>> #e5a50a
 BackgroundColor<<documented>> #273241
 BorderColor<<documented>> #61738a
 FontColor<<documented>> #b8c4d4
}
skinparam note {
 BackgroundColor #1b2330
 BorderColor #61738a
 FontColor #e6edf7
}
hide empty description
title DNS lookup: when can a resolver callback no longer touch the lookup?\n(implemented; wifi_dns.c, struct wifi_dns_lookup, owner = SNTP or TLS worker)
state "Armed\ngeneration set, isComplete = false\n(before submission: inline callbacks are accepted)" as Armed
state "Submitted\nisSubmitted = true, identifier" as Submitted
state "Address seen\naddressIsValid" as AddressSeen
state "Complete\nfirst terminal result wins: 0, -ENOENT,\n-ETIMEDOUT, -EHOSTUNREACH" as Complete
state "Released\nisSubmitted = false; no callback can run" as Released
[*] --> Armed
Armed --> Submitted : dns_get_addr_info (owner lock not held)
Armed --> Complete : inline callback (cached or numeric name)
Submitted --> AddressSeen : callback with address [owner: current generation]
AddressSeen --> Complete : callback: done
Submitted --> Complete : callback: error or timeout
Submitted --> Released : worker leaves on cancel or deadline:\ndns_cancel_addr_info returns 0 or -ENOENT
AddressSeen --> Released : cancel or deadline
Complete --> Released : release
Released --> [*] : context may be reused
note right of Released
 Callbacks run under the resolver lock and are rejected unless the owner's
 generation is current. Cancel under that lock establishes callback quiescence
 before the owner reuses the context. No defect found.
end note
@enduml
